BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 760 Tm (Report on the Corvin Ferry Papers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 728 Tm (Arthur Corvin and Felix Garrow ran the ferry business as partners until 1929.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 712 Tm (The Corvin Ferry Company kept its books at the North Pier office in Gullhaven.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 696 Tm (Silas Thorne, a pilot employed by the Corvin Ferry Company, described the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 680 Tm (winter crossings in a long letter dated March 1928.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 664 Tm (Silas Thorne wrote to Rupert Vane about the loss of the old landing stage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 648 Tm (Ruth Garrow, daughter of Felix Garrow, donated a box of photographs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 632 Tm (Mr. Garrow is remembered in Gullhaven for the brass bell on the ferry.) Tj ET
